//! §3.1/§3.3 — the async `Wallet` handle: `create` / `open` / `close`.
//!
//! This is the consumer that drives the crash-atomic store (store.rs) over the
//! single-writer lock (lifecycle.rs `WalletLock`) and the lifecycle state machine
//! (lifecycle.rs `Lifecycle`). The provisioning / open work is **blocking** (file
//! opens, SQLCipher key setup, the schemerz migrator) so it ALL runs inside
//! `tokio::task::spawn_blocking` — off the Dart/UI thread AND off the async
//! runtime (rust-patterns § Async; spec §7). The handle owns nothing async itself
//! except the seam to the blocking pool.
//!
//! **Exclusive single-writer (§3.3):** `create`/`open` acquire the `WalletLock`
//! FIRST, inside the blocking task, and hold it for the life of the handle —
//! `Drop` releases it (the DB connection closes first, then the lock, by field
//! order). A second opener (this process or another) is REJECTED with
//! `WalletAlreadyOpen` — rejected IS the contract, not "rejected or safe".
//!
//! **Vault injection seam (testability):** the public `create`/`open` resolve the
//! platform key vault ([`platform_vault`]) and forward to the crate-internal
//! `*_with_vault` constructors. Unit tests drive the `_with_vault` path with an
//! in-memory `TestVault` so the host's real Keystore/Keychain is never touched;
//! the platform-vault SELECTION itself is device-E2E territory (owed to a runner,
//! like the custody selftest). Off-vault platforms (headless desktop, for now)
//! fail closed with `VaultAbsent` — the honest degrade, never a silent
//! in-memory wrap key (§4.3a).
//!
//! **Scope:** create / open / close + the migrate-up-at-open (inc-2b-ii-B), and
//! `current_address` — the first read `&self` method, deriving the default UA from
//! the held seed offline (inc-2c-i). Sync is wired (inc-2c-iv-d-3-b-ii): the handle
//! retains `endpoint`/`tor`/`birthday` (§3.2a) and drives the `LightdSyncEngine` over
//! a `SyncController` (`start_sync`/`stop_sync`). The remaining `&self` API surface
//! (`snapshot`/`balance`/`send`/`reveal_mnemonic`/…, §3.1) + `wipe` + the live FRB
//! stream surface arrive with the read surface (d-3-b-iii) / the send engine (inc-2d);
//! `broadcast_jitter` is retained on `Inner` for the send path (consumed at inc-2d-3-a).

